id: CTB-SRC0009-A-1
source: SRC-0009
section: §1.1,§1.2,§1.3,§3.1,§3.2,§8.3
kind: requirement
scope: ARC
title: Complete intended architecture before sequencing
applied-in: STG-00 #1
text: Design, implement and evolve LUXORA Ω∞ as a complete, universal, technology-agnostic, self-maintaining and continuously evolving platform. Do not optimize for a minimum viable architecture, temporary implementation, isolated subsystem or short-term demonstration. The complete intended architecture must be established before implementation sequencing is determined. The architecture must comprehensively cover constitutional foundations, knowledge and assimilation, identity, organizations, tenancy, business composition, configuration, rules, users, experience journeys, catalog, discovery, pricing, promotions, commerce, checkout, payments, wallets, billing, finance, accounting, orders, inventory, logistics, fulfilment, returns, communication, integrations, intelligence, analytics, security, operations, deployment, disaster recovery and platform governance. The architecture must remain open to future domains and capabilities without requiring redesign of its foundations. The objective is not to repeatedly repair and audit a collection of partial systems. The objective is to engineer one coherent, universal platform whose architecture continuously maintains and evolves its own completeness and consistency.
